{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-inertia}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:419b17c344e9ae0de98b234661b29a6d4156d1022f17faa24e7119b92a5c1996", "source_text": "Inertia stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc81dd06d12d0fffb9eb759d767641978053bff07f98a127473e86e4d79968ba", "unit_id": "tag:050P:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-section-the-inertia-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-section-inertia}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0100eab6ff87ac5071c482b860974fe0af84edf18111758e483be94fcda59bad", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe (relative) inertia stack of a stack in groupoids is defined in\nStacks, Section <REF_0001>.\nThe actual construction, in the setting of fibred categories, and some\nof its properties is in\nCategories, Section <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0731e2170b110cdb414518660f651aff4518a434883fa57e785f12d9215b6e2", "unit_id": "tag:050P:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{X}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-inertia}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c6709fa24b5c7707bd986ea03e8886ca94e639888a34ca5ea7ba2f4e51c2e080", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:da2c1689915238d9b034799b5b6093169308e93fc827f95a0ce949eb8d70a9ee", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Then the inertia stack\n<MATH_0002> is an algebraic stack as well.\nThe morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nis representable by algebraic spaces and locally of finite type.\nMore generally, let <MATH_0004> be a morphism\nof algebraic stacks. Then the relative inertia\n<MATH_0005> is an algebraic stack and the\nmorphism\n<MATH_0006>\nis representable by algebraic spaces and locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b5abeccfff7fc1080ac62dc3b5c312d73e902d9bbcc97fe7796ea92c10671cae", "unit_id": "tag:050Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "categories.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 242287, "start": 242277}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242359, "start": 242149}, "container_hash": "sha256:5e5c65214fc77b4f09f86b1bce6c25714697de4be2e8e78c1a2637d6f027befe"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 242783, "start": 242773}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242847, "start": 242659}, "container_hash": "sha256:c56690e42ba08b833426b2187a56e6527ac6172fb9b61653b212c3400b48a67f"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 243361, "start": 243351}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 243453, "start": 243199}, "container_hash": "sha256:22bd2849d377c2382ec7d8e17d3577c7f8754022db5b490d58106c1c7300a2de"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "categories-section-inertia", "owner_tag": "04Z2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:4108cf525225a3a755d96ea80bf1b4fb421350b56ee9543c0b8ab97e2eaa3f9f", "source_label": "categories-section-inertia", "usage": "quad-connector", "usage_source": {"after": "\\quad", "before": "\\quad", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "connective-and", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 127, "start": 124}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "and"}], "source": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\Delta, \\mathcal{X} \\times_S \\mathcal{X}, \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{X}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}} \\to\n\\mathcal{X}\n\\times_{\\Delta, \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}, \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{X}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 375, "start": 105}, "source_hash": "sha256:9665ccf55be31c2f9d79608dfcebcc621fce4dcd958f5960024ca4762e5aaae2"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\Delta, \\mathcal{X} \\times_S \\mathcal{X}, \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{X}\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}} \\to\n\\mathcal{X}\n\\times_{\\Delta, \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}, \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$T \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$2$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x) \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\\\\nT \\ar[r]^x & \\mathcal{X}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x)$", "MATH_0009": "$T$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x) \\ar[d] &\nK \\ar[l] \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{Y}(f(x), f(x)) &\nT \\ar[l]_-e \\ar[r]^x & \\mathcal{X}\n}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$2$", "MATH_0013": "$T$", "MATH_0014": "$K$", "MATH_0015": "$K \\to T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-inertia-fibred-category}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-isom-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{categories-lemma-relative-inertia-as-fibre-product}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-permanence-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf6687fc9a8eb3aeacc29b42fe6abda39e21a66644ae9091626afeedca896770", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:105ed2b6448eeb9f94bac8bc8547b14e4027c3af54d92b2b0a5add9f2eee4866", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc031e9aa8e2abeae2319ed8e0da149598327dd2efd91f264d4afed61f3ce234", "source_text": "By\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthere are equivalences\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nwhich shows that the inertia stacks are algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism given by\nthe object <MATH_0002> of the fibre category of <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004>.\nThen we get a <MATH_0005>-fibre product square\n<MATH_0006>\nThis follows immediately from the definition of <MATH_0007>.\nSince <MATH_0008> is always an algebraic space\nlocally of finite type over <MATH_0009> (see\nLemma <REF_0002>)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0010> is representable\nby algebraic spaces and locally of finite type. Finally, for\nthe relative inertia we get\n<MATH_0011>\nwith both squares <MATH_0012>-fibre products. This follows from\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThe left vertical arrow is a morphism of algebraic spaces locally of finite\ntype over <MATH_0013>, and hence is locally of finite type, see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nThus <MATH_0014> is an algebraic space and <MATH_0015> is locally of finite type.\nThis proves the assertion on the relative inertia.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:078ea450f04445d1aa1ba751ef44b11f84d6ef9eb3a8d227b4c05bf892b71036", "unit_id": "tag:050Q:proof"}
